 "description": "GLM 5.3's TP-split adoption (85893d6f1 to 4334c4cdc): the 288 routed experts are split across the ranks instead of 72 per rank, and each MoE sublayer's all-reduce runs on F32 partials rounded once. The EP routed cubins give way to the split ones and two F32 comm cubins; each rank allocates five F32 all-reduce buffers at create; route tables, sorted rows and the expert intermediate follow the 288 local experts; the KDA anchor items grow from 8 to 16 (conv, delta and indexer state planes and the drafter's retained rows); NVFP4 expert scales are admitted for all 288 experts. Written after the change landed.",
